{
 "title": "SMPTE ST 2065-2 Academy Printing Density (APD) spectral responsivities",
 "description": "Pi_APD red/green/blue channel responsivities (Table A.1, normative) and the influx spectrum S_APD (Table B.1, informative), as tabulated. Pi_APD already incorporates the influx (a Bell & Howell Model C lamp house through a Wratten 2B), so density is D = -log10(integral(Pi T) / integral(Pi)) with Pi alone; S_APD is carried for reference only. Target metric of the ADX (ST 2065-3) route.",
 "units": "relative responsivity, peak = 1.0 per channel as published; influx relative spectral power as published",
 "wavelength_range_nm": [
  360.0,
  730.0
 ],
 "sampling_nm": 2,
 "geometry": "ISO 5-2 diffuse transmission (ST 2065-2 section 5)",
 "provenance": "Transcribed 2026-08-28 from SMPTE ST 2065-2:2012 (pub.smpte.org/doc/st2065-2/20120312-pub/st2065-2-2012.pdf), Annex A Table A.1 and Annex B Table B.1, by text extraction of the PDF; every one of the 186 wavelengths recovered exactly once per table, two rows duplicated verbatim by the extractor and de-duplicated after an equality check. The 2020 edition was not fetchable (access denied) and was not compared. The PDF is not held in the repository.",
 "peak_wavelengths_nm": {
  "red": 692,
  "green": 550,
  "blue": 466
 },
 "notes": "Differs from RP 180 (data/standards/RP180_responsivities.json): 2 nm sampling against 10 nm, and sub-400 nm blue content of 0.21% of the blue integral (RP 180: ~3.5%). ST 2065-2 note 3 warns that conversions from scanner density to APD are imperfect; this repository reaches APD by spectral synthesis from the traced dye basis, not by a matrix, and the Vision3 basis grid starts at 402 nm, so the sub-402 nm share is truncated and the responsivity renormalized (bounded bias; see the engine's report line).",
